<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section-big faq">
  <h2 class="sec-mid reveal">The fine print, on request.</h2>
  <div class="faq-list reveal d1">
    <details>
      <summary>Where do the names come from?<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary>
      <p>A decision-maker is named only when a credible public source backs the name, and the pitch links what was read. Every name is rated — confirmed, likely or unverified. No source, no name: the role is returned blank instead.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will it invent facts?<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary>
      <p>No. Numbers come from your brief or a cited source; anything else becomes a bracketed placeholder, listed for you to fill. Every draft is read back against your banned terms before you see it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How does my team get in?<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary>
      <p>Pay with your work email and every colleague on your domain signs straight in — no seats to count. Sign-in is Google or an emailed single-use link; there are no passwords.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What happens to my data?<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary>
      <p>Workspaces are strictly separated — your research, pitches and network are visible to your team only. Email addresses in a LinkedIn export are deleted at import, and your network never travels on a shared pitch. The <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> says the rest, plainly.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What if it's not for us?<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary>
      <p>Money back if it doesn't earn its keep — no trial theater. And if you want ten thousand scraped emails, this isn't it: the studio goes deep on a shortlist worth pitching.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

